							<div align="center"><font color="#0000ff"><b>Bard Epic</b></font><br /> </div> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody><tr><td class="ContentBoxBody">Start of the quest</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">The Bard Epic quest starts and ends in the Dreadlands. You talk to a guy named Baldric Slezaf located in the area near the Druid and Wizard portals, inside one of the pyramids in the ancient ruins. His location is 773, 9666. Talk with him and he will tell you about two missing pages from his symphony and an instrument to play it on. If you bring him the items he talks about, he will give you your reward - the Singing Short Sword.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <br /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Maestro's Symphony - Top Half of Page 24 (1)</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">West Karana - Talk to Konia Swiftfoot at Guard Tower 1 and volunteer to participate in her relay race - Receive a Torch</td></tr></tbody> </table> <br /> <hr id="null" /> <br /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Maestro's Symphony - Top Half of Page 24 (2)</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Misty Thicket - Give the Torch to Fajio Knejo near the entrance to Runnyeye Citadel - Receive another Torch</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <br /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Maestro's Symphony - Top Half of Page 24 (3)</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Lake Rathetear - Give the Torch to Misty Tekchita near the entrance to the Arena - Receive a ring called Proof of Speed</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <br /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Maestro's Symphony - Top Half of Page 24 (4)</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Lake Rathetear - Give the Torch to Misty Tekchita near the entrance to the Arena - Receive a ring called Proof of Speed</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Maestro's Symphony - Top Half of Page 24 (5)</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">West Karana - Give the Proof of Speed to Konia Swiftfoot - Receive Maestro's Symphony - Top Half of Page 24 and this will begin the next step of the quest</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Maestro's Symphony - Bottom Half of Page 24 (1)</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">South Karana - Talk to Braenar Swiftsong at the well and ask him "what doll?" - Receive a Solusek Mining Company Invoice</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Maestro's Symphony - Bottom Half of Page 24 (2)</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Solusek A - Give the Solusek Mining Company Invoice to the gnome merchant Marfen Binkdirple - Receive A Mechanical Doll</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Maestro's Symphony - Bottom Half of Page 24 (3)</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Estate of Unrest - Give A Mechanical Doll to Braenar's daughter Serra (through underwater channel at right of the mansion, she is next to the Gnome Spelunker) - Receive A Note for Braenar</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Maestro's Symphony - Bottom Half of Page 24 (4)</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">South Karana - Give the Note to Braenar - Receive another Note</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Maestro's Symphony - Bottom Half of Page 24 (5)</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">West Karana - Find Maligar (+1300 , -11500). It is suggested to kill his friends then give him the Note. This will cause Maligar's Estranged Doppleganger to spawn. Kill both Maligar and Maligar's Estranged Doppleganger and loot Maligar's Head. NOTES: (1179, -10878). His spawn is every 30 minutes or so, not bad, if you mess up (turn the head into the wrong guy), you can try again in a bit. After you give Maligar the note, he will spawn his Maligars Enraged Doppleganger. Maligar says 'Hmmm. What's this? A note from that silly bard Baenar? I wasn't aware that those of his kind could write, much less read.' Maligar lets out a deep laugh. 'I see you do not share my sense of humor. Let's read it, shall we? Oh, no! She's dead? I knew that already, you fool. It was by my hand she died! Ooops! Did I let that slip out? Silly me. I guess I will have to kill you now!' Maligar and his whole camps faction can be changed using lvl 11 song, Cinda's Charismatic Carillon, especially effective using the Dark Elf mask, I've heard it doesn't work without one. I was told at the time to charm him, so my experience is below... When I killed Maligar and his Doppleganger, it was myself, a 47 bard, a 51 bard, a 53 wizzie, and a 45 druid. We pulled Maligar's friends first, who went down easily one by one. They do not aggro if you pull one by one. Then we charmed Maligar, ordered him to sit down, his Doppleganger spawned, and even though I was twisting resist songs, we still were blinded. If your Magic Resist is high enough (like over 150 MR) and you're high enough level, you should resist being blinded. I did resist the Fear spell though. As of September 2001, I hear reports that he no longer blinds, so maybe he was nerfed a bit... Anyway back when I did Maligar, I had my chants memmed, since I knew I was going to be blinded, so I had my target, and hopefully was able to get him a few times with my DoTs. From what I heard from the druid helping us, was that the Doppleganger was smart and blinded everyone he could. It was a very close fight, we brought him down though, and then charmed Maligar again, and got our second Maligar Doppleganger's head. Once you kill the doppleganger, loot his head. Unless you want to kill Maligar, you can run at this point to the zone.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Maestro's Symphony - Bottom Half of Page 24 (6)</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">South Karana - Give Maligar's Head to Braenar Swiftsong - Receive Mahlin's Bongos</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Maestro's Symphony - Bottom Half of Page 24 (7)</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">West Karana - Give Mahlin's Bongos to Konia Swiftwind - Receive Maestro's Symphony - Bottom Half of Page 24</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Maestro's Symphony - Page 25 (1)</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">South Karana - Talk to Kelkim Mekia to begin the next step of the quest for Maestro's Symphony - Page 25 NOTES: she is between the centaurs and treants along the zone line that is a "drop-off". Hail her to start the conversation and quest details. You say: 'Hail, Kelkim Menkia' Kelkim Menkia sighs as she looks over her lute. My lute was mangled by those damnable gnolls. I have no idea how I'm going to get a new set of strings for it. They were so rare. You say: 'What rare Strings?' Kelkim Menkia says 'I only use the finest lute strings on my lute. My uncle got them for me from across the world. His name was Zendrik the Wurmslayer. As his name implies, he killed many wurms and drakes. The strings for my lute were all made from the guts of the wurms and drakes he slew.' You say: 'What wurms and drakes?' Kelkim Menkia says ' The strings were from a chromodrac, a red wurm, and a huge onyx drake. It always sounded so wonderful.' Kelkim sighs, looking off into the horizon. As she shakes her lute angrily, she says, "I'll kill all of you dirty gnolls!"</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Maestro's Symphony - Page 25 (2)</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Skyfire Mountains - Kill everything around +500, -4000 to spawn Eldrig the Old , a named chromatic drake. Kill Eldrig the Old and loot the Chromatic Guts. *Note: Eldrig the Old can summon, dispell and cast Boiling Blood DoT.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Maestro's Symphony - Page 25 (3)</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Burning Woods - Kill everything around -450, -2550 to spawn Nezekezena, a named red wurm. Kill Nezekezena and loot the Red Wurm Guts. *Note: Nezekezena can summon and gate.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Maestro's Symphony - Page 25 (4)</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Rathe Mountains - Kill all lizards, drakes, basiliks, etc. near the sphinx to spawn Blackwing, a huge onyx drake. Kill Blackwing and loot the Huge Onyx Drake Guts. *Note: Beware of Zazamouhk, an evil enchanter sphinx and Rharzar, a level 55 green drake</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Maestro's Symphony - Page 25 (5)</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">South Karana - Give Kelkim Mekia the Chromatic Guts, Red Wurm Guts and Huge Onyx Drake Guts - Receive Maestro's Symphony - Page 25</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Forpar's Note (1)</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Butcherblock Mountains - You must find and talk to Vedico Windwisper in one of the shops at the docks. Forpar Fizfla will not talk to you until you help his friend Vedico. She lost her horn to a cyclops named Quag Maelstrome and wants your help in retrieving it. *Note: Quag casts mana drain.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Forpar's Note 2</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Ocean of Tears - Find Quag Maelstrom on the Seafury Cyclops island. Kill Quag and loot the Alluring Horn.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Forpar's Note 3</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Butcherblock Mountains - Give the Alluring Horn to Vedico Windwhisper - Receive a Note for Forpar.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Forpar's Note 4</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Steamfont Mountains - Play Cinda's Charismatic Carillion and give the Note from Vedico to Forpar Fizla near the windmills (+126, -600) - Receive Forpar's Note which lists the 3 things he needs to make a mystical lute.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Mystical Lute Head 1</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Kedge Keep - Find Phinigel Autropos, a level 50 wizard. Have a high level bard or enchanter who can mezz him and his 6 guardians. Kill Phinigel and loot Backbone of an Ancient Fishman. *Note: Phinigel can dispell, including enduring breath.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Mystical Lute Head 2</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Karnor's Castle - Find and kill a Drolvarg Bodyguard just below the Hand Room to spawn the Drolvarg Warlord. Have a cleric and enchanter if possible, kill the Drolvarg Warlord and loot a Petrified Werewolf Skull. *Note: Warlord can summon.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Mystical Lute Head 3</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Plane of Fear - Find and kill Amalgym Warriors and Knights and loot a Amalgym Tentacle (9/25 1h slashing weapon). *Note: Knights can heal, summon pets, and harmtouch.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Mystical Lute Head 4</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Steamfont Mountains - Give Forpar Fizla the Backbone of an Ancient Fisherman, Petrified Werewolf Skull, Amalgym Tentacle and Forpar's Note - Receive the Mystical Lute Head (head and neck). Ask "what next pieces" to receive the next step in the quest.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Mystical Lute Body 1</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Nagafen's Lair, Solusek B, Skyfire or The Hole - You must acquire a Large Red Dragon Scale from ONE of four dragons: Lord Nagafen in Nagafen's Lair, Zordakilicus Ragefire in Solusek B, Talendor of Skyfire or Nortlav Scalekeeper in The Hole.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Mystical Lute Body 2</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">The Dreadlands or Permafrost - You must acquire a Large White Dragon Scale from ONE of two dragons: Gorenaire in The Dreadlands or Lady Vox in Permafrost.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Mystical Lute Body 3</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">You must acquire 1 (one) Metal Bits from someone with a Smithing Tradeskill, trivial 21</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Mystical Lute Body 4</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Steamfont Mountains - Give Forpar Fizla the Large Red Dragon Scale, Large White Dragon Scale and 1 (one) Metal Bits - Receive the Mystical Lute Body</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Mystical Lute Strings (Trakanon's Guts) 1</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Sebilis - Go to Trakanon's Lair. Talk to the Undead Bard and give him the Mystical Lute Body. He will hand it back to you and attack you. Kill the Undead Bard to spawn the clone of Trakanon. Kill the clone of Trakanon and loot Trakanon's Guts. Note: Beware of the clone of Trakanon's breath attack.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Mystical Lute Strings (Trakanon's Guts) 2</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Steamfont Mountains - Give Forpar Fizla Trakanon's Guts, Mystical Lute Head and Mystical Lute Body - Receive Forpar's Mystical Lute</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody><tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">The Sword</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">The Dreadlands - Give Baldric Slezaf the Maestro's Symphony Top of Page 24, Maestro's Symphony Bottom of Page 24, Maestro's Symphony Page 25 and Forpar's Mystical Lute - Receive *The Singing Short Sword*</td></tr></tbody> </table> <br /> 
							
